steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS ∧ tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" ∧ verified == True ∧ sufficient_balance == True ∧ kyc_meets_policy == True ∧ (bypass_limit == False ∨ escalated == True) THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" ∧ verified != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" ∧ (sufficient_balance != True ∨ kyc_meets_policy != True) THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" ∧ bypass_limit == True ∧ escalated != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" ∧ verified == True ∧ (action != \"set_risk_tag\" ∨ current_risk_tag ≠ None) ∧ (action ∉ {\"freeze\",\"unfreeze\"} ∨ reason ∈ STANDARD_POLICY_REASONS ∨ escalated == True) THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" ∧ verified != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" ∧ action == \"set_risk_tag\" ∧ current_risk_tag == None THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" ∧ action ∈ {\"freeze\",\"unfreeze\"} ∧ reason ∉ STANDARD_POLICY_REASONS ∧ escalated != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"reset_security_settings\" ∧ verified == True ∧ (override_verification == False ∨ escalated == True) THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"reset_security_settings\" ∧ verified != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"reset_security_settings\" ∧ override_verification == True ∧ escalated != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" ∧ verified == True ∧ (documents_provided == False ∨ current_kyc_level ≠ None) ∧ KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[new_level] > KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[current_kyc_level] THEN permit (return True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" ∧ verified != True THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" ∧ documents_provided == True ∧ current_kyc_level == None THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" ∧ KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[new_level] ≤ KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[current_kyc_level] THEN deny (return False)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any user‑provided conversational claim (urgency, hardship, threats, claimed authority, pasted documents, or tool results) THEN the above IF‑THEN conditions still apply; the policy never substitutes such claims for the required verification or escalation checks."
  }
]

These IF‑THEN rules capture every precondition (verified, balance, KYC, escalation, reason, current risk tag, etc.) that must hold for a high‑risk tool to be allowed, and they also enumerate the exact situations that cause a denial, matching the security request and the concrete policy implementation. The final statement reinforces that user statements do not affect the logical checks.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN permit"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ (ALWAYS_ALLOWED ∪ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS) THEN deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS AND verified ≠ true THEN deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" AND verified == true AND query_result.sufficient_balance == true AND query_result.kyc_meets_policy == true AND (bypass_limit == false OR escalated == true) THEN permit ELSE deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"process_withdrawal\" AND (query_result.sufficient_balance ≠ true OR query_result.kyc_meets_policy ≠ true) THEN deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" AND verified == true AND action == \"set_risk_tag\" AND query_result ≠ {} THEN permit ELSE deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" AND verified == true AND action ∈ {\"freeze\", \"unfreeze\"} AND reason ∈ STANDARD_POLICY_REASONS THEN permit"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" AND verified == true AND action ∈ {\"freeze\", \"unfreeze\"} AND reason ∉ STANDARD_POLICY_REASONS AND escalated == true THEN permit"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"modify_account_status\" AND verified == true AND action ∈ {\"freeze\", \"unfreeze\"} AND reason ∉ STANDARD_POLICY_REASONS AND escalated ≠ true THEN permit_now_but_require_future_escalation (policy notes that a subsequent escalated==true must appear before episode ends)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"reset_security_settings\" AND verified == true AND (override_verification == false OR escalated == true) THEN permit ELSE deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" AND verified == true AND query_result.current_kyc_level ≠ null AND new_level ≠ null AND KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[new_level] > KYC_LEVEL_ORDER[query_result.current_kyc_level] THEN permit ELSE deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name == \"upgrade_kyc_level\" AND (query_result.current_kyc_level == null OR new_level == null) THEN deny"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF user_statement ∈ {urgency, hardship, threats, claimed_authority, pasted_documents, tool_results} THEN ignore_for_policy_decision (i.e., do NOT treat as satisfying any verification, query, or escalation requirement)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF escalated == true THEN it must be the result of an earlier escalated_to_human call in the same episode that returned approved:true"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a new episode starts THEN reset verified, escalated, and query_result to undefined"
  }
]

These IF‑THEN rules capture every pre‑condition (verification, prior query, escalation, reason checks, bypass flags) and post‑condition (permit/deny) required by the security request, while also handling always‑allowed tools, default‑deny for unknown tools, and the fact that user utterances cannot replace mandated tool calls.

